                  "\n  ",
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{While we're talking about sets, there's an idea that's really useful, which is dividing a set up into a partition.  Let's read exactly what a partition is... }"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Here's a set $S$ - how do I create a partition?  I will draw in some sets.  each one has to be completely inside $S$, and they can't overlap at all.  And I have to make sure I cover all of $S$.}"
