                              },
                              " \n      ",
                              {
                                "vspace": "\\vspace{.5cm}"
                              },
                              "\n      ",
                              {
                                "note": "\\note[item]{Because events are sets, we can combine them with\n        set operations to make new events.  Let's think about what\n        those operations mean.}"
                              },
                              " \n      ",
                              {
                                "note": "\\note[item]{Here's two events for the simple example of a die roll}"
                              },
                              "\n      ",
                              {
                                "note": "\\note[item]{First, think about how you would write down the\n        event A OR B?  that is, either A occurs or B occurs.}"
                              },
                              " \n      ",
                              {
                                "note": "\\note[item]{Well, that means that the outcome that occurs must\n        be in at least one of A or B, so it must be in their union.\n        When you see a union, think OR.}"
                              },
                              " \n      ",
                              "\n      ",
                              "\n      ",
                              {
                                "itemize": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "\\begin{itemize}"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "\n  ",
                                    {
                                      "setlength": "\\setlength"
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "itemsep": "\\itemsep{1em}"
                                    },
                                    "\n      ",
                                    {
                                      "item": "\\item"
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "item": "\\item"
