            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "section": "\\section{Deriving Properties of Probability}"
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{A Helpful Analogy}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "center": "\\center"
                  },
                  " ",
                  {
                    "textbf": "\\textbf{Probability $\\Longleftrightarrow$ Area}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  "\n      ",
                  {
                    "includegraphics": "\\includegraphics[width=.6\\textwidth]{figures/sample_space}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{The amazing thing about probability is that with just 3\n    axioms, you can prove all the other properties that you expect\n    based on your intuition.  But it can be tough to find a solution\n    just by staring at equations.}"
                  },
                  " \n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Here's an analogy that may help you.}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Probabilities are a lot like areas.  Actually, area is\n    also a type of measure in mathematics - most of the structure is\n    the same.}"
                  },
                  " \n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{If you just have a few events, it can help to draw them\n    as areas.  That's not a proof, but it can give you an idea of how\n    they behave.}"
                  },
                  " \n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Let's think about the sample space as a square\n    dartboard.  We'll define its area to be 1.  I'm really bad at\n    darts so every point is just as likely as any other point.}"
                  },
                  " \n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{An event is some shape on the dartboard.  so the\n    probability that the dart lands in the shape is its area. A\n    picture like this can help you figure out a tricky proof.}"
                  },
                  " \n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{The Subset Subtraction Rule}"
                  },
                  "\n  Given ",
                  {
                    "$": [
                      {
                        "begin": "$"
                      },
                      [
                        "A,B ",
                        {
                          "in": "\\in"
                        },
                        " S"
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "$"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  ", ",
                  {
                    "$": [
                      {
                        "begin": "$"
                      },
                      [
                        "A ",
                        {
                          "subseteq": "\\subseteq"
                        },
                        " B"
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "$"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  ".  Compute ",
                  {
                    "$": [
                      {
                        "begin": "$"
                      },
                      [
                        "P(B",
                        {
                          "setminus": "\\setminus"
                        },
                        " A)"
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "$"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  ".\n  \n  Ex: A = being over 7', B = being over 6'.\n\n\n   ",
                  {
                    "includegraphics": "\\includegraphics[width=.6\\textwidth]{figures/sample_space}"
                  },
                  "\n   ",
                  "\n   ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Let's start with a simple property, if we assume that\n     event A is a subset of event B, what's the probability if we\n     subtract A from B.}"
                  },
                  " \n   ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{For example, if A is the event of being over 7 foot\n     tall, and B is the event of being over 6 foot tall.  how do you\n     get the probability of being between 6 and 7 foot tall?}"
                  },
                  " \n   ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{I'll draw a circle for B and a circle for A.  To apply\n     the probability axioms, we need disjoint sets.  A and B are not\n     disjoint, but we know how to partition $B$.  Remember our\n     partition rule 1 from earlier.}"
                  },
                  " \n   ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{ $ B = (B\\setminus A) \\cup ( A \\cap B) =  (B\\setminus A) \\cup  A  \\implies P(B) = P(B\\setminus A)+ P(A)$}"
                  },
                  "\n ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Also, by axiom 1, $P(B\\setminus A) \\geq 0$ so $P(B) \\geq\n   P(A)$}"
                  },
                  " \n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}[t]"
                },
                [
                  "t",
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{The Complement Rule}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Given the subtraction rule, you can very quickly solve\n    for the complement rule}"
                  },
                  " \n  Given ",
                  {
                    "$": [
                      {
                        "begin": "$"
                      },
                      [
                        "A ",
                        {
                          "in": "\\in"
                        },
                        " S"
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "$"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  ".  Compute ",
                  {
                    "$": [
                      {
                        "begin": "$"
                      },
                      [
                        "P(A^C)"
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "$"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  ".\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Note $A \\subseteq S$.}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{subtraction rule $\\implies  P(A\\setminus S) = P(S) - P(A)$}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Axiom 2: $P(S) = 1$}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{$P(A^C) = 1 - P(A)$}"
                  },
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n",
                  "%  \\frametitle{Fundamental Components of Probability Space}",
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "alertblock": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{alertblock}{Basic Properties of Probability}"
                      },
                      [
                        "Basic Properties of Probability",
                        "\n    ",
                        {
                          "footnotesize": "\\footnotesize"
                        },
                        " Given a probability space ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "(",
                              {
                                "Omega": "\\Omega"
                              },
                              ", S, P)"
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        ", For all events ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "A, B ",
                              {
                                "in": "\\in"
                              },
                              " S"
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        " : \n    ",
                        {
                          "align*": [
                            {
                              "begin": "\\begin{align*}"
                            },
                            [
                              "\n      ",
                              {
                                "tag": "\\tag{\\textit{Monotonicity}}"
                              },
                              "\n      ",
                              "& ",
                              {
                                "text": "\\text{If }"
                              },
                              " A ",
                              {
                                "subseteq": "\\subseteq"
                              },
                              " B",
                              {
                                "text": "\\text{, then }"
                              },
                              "P(A) ",
                              {
                                "leq": "\\leq"
                              },
                              " P(B) ",
                              "\\\\",
                              " \n      ",
                              {
                                "tag": "\\tag{\\textit{Subtraction}}"
                              },
                              "\n      ",
                              "& ",
                              {
                                "text": "\\text{If }"
                              },
                              " A ",
                              {
                                "subseteq": "\\subseteq"
                              },
                              " B",
                              {
                                "text": "\\text{, then the probability\n                   assigned to }"
                              },
                              "B ",
                              "\\\\",
                              " ",
                              "&  ",
                              {
                                "text": "\\text{\\hspace{1em} but not }"
                              },
                              "A,\n                                       ",
                              {
                                "text": "\\text{written }"
                              },
                              "P(B",
                              {
                                "textbackslash": "\\textbackslash"
                              },
                              " A) = P(B) - P(A) ",
                              "\\\\",
                              " \n      ",
                              {
                                "tag": "\\tag{\\textit{Probability Bounds}}"
                              },
                              "\n                 ",
                              "& 0 ",
                              {
                                "leq": "\\leq"
                              },
                              " P(A) ",
                              {
                                "leq": "\\leq"
                              },
                              " 1 ",
                              "\\\\",
                              "\n      ",
                              {
                                "tag": "\\tag{\\textit{Compliments}}"
                              },
                              "\n                 ",
                              "& P(A^",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "C"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              ") = 1 - P(A)  ",
                              "\\\\",
                              " \n    "
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "\\end{align*}"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        "\n",
                        "\n    ",
                        {
                          "note": "\\note[item]{Here's the theorem from the textbook, with a few extra\n      results.  You can see how we're starting to build up more tools\n      we can use.}"
                        },
                        " \n    ",
                        {
                          "note": "\\note[item]{\\paul{Possibly end with a statement of the addition\n        rule, then \"you'll see a proof for this in the next\n        exercise.\"}}"
                        },
                        " \n    ",
                        "\n    ",
                        "% \\begin{itemize}",
                        "\n    ",
                        "% \\item If A $\\subseteq B$, then $P(A) \\leq P(B)$ (\\textit{Monotonicity})",
                        "\n    ",
                        "% \\item If $A \\subseteq B$ then the probability",
                        "\n    ",
                        "%   assigned to $B$ but not $A = P(B) - P(A)$ (\\textit{Subtraction})",
                        "\n    ",
                        "% \\item $0 \\leq P(A) \\leq 1$ (\\textit{Probability Bounds})",
                        "\n    ",
                        "% \\item $P(A^{C}) = 1 - P(A)$ (\\textit{Compliments}",
                        "\n    ",
                        "% \\end{itemize}",
                        "\n  "
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{alertblock}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  "% talk through the \"simple terms\" ",
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "section": "\\section{Learnosity Concept Check - Addition Rule}"
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\nHere is a proof of the addition rule, select the best justification for each line.\n",
                  {
                    "align*": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{align*}"
                      },
                      [
                        "\nA ",
                        {
                          "cup": "\\cup"
                        },
                        " B &=  (A ",
                        {
                          "setminus": "\\setminus"
                        },
                        " B) ",
                        {
                          "cup": "\\cup"
                        },
                        " ",
                        "(A ",
                        {
                          "cap": "\\cap"
                        },
                        " B) ",
                        {
                          "cup": "\\cup"
                        },
                        " ",
                        "(B ",
                        {
                          "setminus": "\\setminus"
                        },
                        " A) ",
                        "\\\\",
                        "\nP(A ",
                        {
                          "cup": "\\cup"
                        },
                        " B) &= P(A ",
                        {
                          "setminus": "\\setminus"
                        },
                        " B) + P(A ",
                        {
                          "cap": "\\cap"
                        },
                        " B) +  P(B ",
                        {
                          "setminus": "\\setminus"
                        },
                        " A) ",
                        "\\\\",
                        "\n",
                        "&= P(A ",
                        {
                          "setminus": "\\setminus"
                        },
                        " B) + P(A ",
                        {
                          "cap": "\\cap"
                        },
                        " B) +  P(B ",
                        {
                          "setminus": "\\setminus"
                        },
                        " A) + P(A ",
                        {
                          "cap": "\\cap"
                        },
                        " B) - P(A ",
                        {
                          "cap": "\\cap"
                        },
                        " B) ",
                        "\\\\",
                        "\n",
                        "&=  P",
                        {
                          "big(": "\\big("
                        },
                        " ",
                        "(A ",
                        {
                          "setminus": "\\setminus"
                        },
                        " B) ",
                        {
                          "cup": "\\cup"
                        },
                        "( A ",
                        {
                          "cap": "\\cap"
                        },
                        " B) ",
                        {
                          "big)": "\\big)"
                        },
                        " +  P",
                        {
                          "big(": "\\big("
                        },
                        " ",
                        "(B ",
                        {
                          "setminus": "\\setminus"
                        },
                        " A) ",
                        {
                          "cup": "\\cup"
                        },
                        " ",
                        "(A ",
                        {
                          "cap": "\\cap"
                        },
                        " B) ",
                        {
                          "big)": "\\big)"
                        },
                        " - P(A ",
                        {
                          "cap": "\\cap"
                        },
                        " B)",
                        "\\\\",
                        "\n",
                        "&= P(A) + P(B)  - P(A ",
                        {
                          "cap": "\\cap"
                        },
                        " B)\n"
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{align*}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "\n",
                  "\n",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{\\paul{This isn't perfect yet.  I think what's needed is to build up a few basic set properties first and name them.  For example, establish a name for $(A \\setminus B ) \\cup (A \\cap B) = A$}}"
                  },
                  "\n",
