            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "section": "\\section{Learnosity Concept Check - Applying the Addition Rule}"
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Applying the Addition Rule}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  "\n  A station along Route 66 sells gas and postcards.  The probability that a customer buys postcards is .4.  The probability that a customer leaves without buying anything is .3.  The probability that the customer buys both gas and postcards is .2.  What is the probability that the customer buys gas?\n  \n  ",
                  {
                    "paul": "\\paul{Answer: .5}"
                  },
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "%",
            "\n",
            "%\\begin{frame}",
            "\n",
            "%  \\frametitle{Joint Probability Introduction and Reading}",
            "\n",
            "%  \\begin{itemize}",
            "\n",
            "%  \\item Useful predictions use information to be more accurate than",
            "\n",
            "%    long-run population averages ",
            "\n",
            "%  \\item Predicting the next word written in a phone email system",
            "\n",
            "%  \\item Build toward this from probability axioms ",
            "\n",
            "%  \\end{itemize}",
            "\n",
            "%  \\textbf{Reading Assignment:}",
            "\n",
            "%  Read from \\textbf{1.1.3 Joint and Conditional Probabilities} on page",
            "\n",
            "%  9 to the bottom of page 10. ",
            "\n",
            "%\\end{frame}",
            "\n",
            "%",
            "\n",
            "%\\begin{frame}",
            "\n",
            "%  \\frametitle{Example 1.1.6: Flipping Coins and Rolling Dice }",
            "\n",
            "%  \\begin{exampleblock}{Example 1.1.6: a fair dice roll}",
            "\n",
            "%    Suppose that you are interested in the probability that two events",
            "\n",
            "%    occur while rolling a single die.",
            "\n",
            "%    \\begin{itemize}",
            "\n",
            "%    \\item Let Event $A: \\text{the face is} \\geq 4; \\omega \\in \\{4,5,6\\}$",
            "\n",
            "%    \\item Let Event $B: \\text{the face is even}; \\omega \\in \\{4, 6\\}$",
            "\n",
            "%    \\end{itemize}",
            "\n",
            "%    To answer this: $P(A \\cap B) = P(\\{4,5,6\\} \\cap \\{4,6\\}) =",
            "\n",
            "%    P(\\{4,6\\})$. Since each of the faces has the same probability",
            "\n",
            "%    mapping, $1/6$, and the cardinality of the outcomes that meet the",
            "\n",
            "%    joint condition is 2, $\\frac{1}{6} |\\{4,6\\}| = \\mathbf{1/3}$. ",
            "\n",
            "%  \\end{exampleblock}",
            "\n",
            "%\\end{frame}",
            "\n",
            "%",
            "\n",
            "%\\begin{frame}",
            "\n",
            "%  \\frametitle{Attending the Final Game of the World Series}",
            "\n",
            "%  \\begin{exampleblock}{The World Series}",
            "\n",
            "%    Pick a sport that you like\u2014maybe soccer, baseball, basketball, tennis,",
            "\n",
            "%    or cricket\u2014and suppose that you would like to go to the world",
            "\n",
            "%    championships. \\\\ \\vspace{1em} The championships are best of seven series\u2014the",
            "\n",
            "%    first team to win four wins all. \\textit{Suppose that because",
            "\n",
            "%      you're busy with MIDS, you can only attend one game, and you",
            "\n",
            "%      would like it to be the game where a new champion is crowned.}",
            "\n",
            "%    For which game should you buy tickets?",
            "\n",
            "%    \\begin{enumerate}",
            "\n",
            "%      \\item What are the events? ",
            "\n",
            "%      \\item What are the combinations of events that must hold for the",
            "\n",
            "%        contest to end on Game 5? ",
            "\n",
            "%      \\item What is the probability that the event ends on Game 5? ",
            "\n",
            "%    \\end{enumerate} ",
            "\n",
            "%  \\end{exampleblock}",
            "\n",
            "%\\end{frame}",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "section": "\\section{Conditional Probability}"
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Conditional Probability, Part I}"
                  },
                  "\n  Conditional probability is a rescoping of the sample space from\n  ",
                  {
                    "$": [
                      {
                        "begin": "$"
                      },
                      [
                        {
                          "Omega": "\\Omega"
                        }
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "$"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "\u2014every possible outcome\u2014to a smaller set called the\n  ",
                  {
                    "textit": "\\textit{conditioning set}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "itemize": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{itemize}"
                      },
                      [
                        "\n  ",
                        {
                          "item": "\\item"
                        },
                        {
                          "item": "\\item"
                        }
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{itemize}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "\n  Uses information to produce a ",
                  {
                    "textit": "\\textit{better}"
                  },
                  " statement of the\n  likelihood of an event\n  \n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{\\paul{A lot of text here.  how about instead: \"Idea: How probable an event is changes with more information.\" and skip text at bottom?}}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{\\paul{Or end with: how can we represent probabilities when we have extra information?}}"
                  },
                  "\n",
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Think of a Dartboard...}"
                  },
                  "\n      ",
                  {
                    "center": "\\center"
                  },
                  "  ",
                  {
                    "includegraphics": "\\includegraphics[width = 0.9\\linewidth]{./figures/vt}"
                  },
                  "\n",
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Let's build up some intuition by thinking about the dartboard analogy.}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Event V for volleyball player is an area on the board.}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{If all you know is that the dart hit the board randomly, the probability that it's in V is the area of V divided by the area of the entire sample space (which we assume to be 1).}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Now what if I tell you that the dart landed somewhere in T, meaning tall?  What does your intuition say?}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Well, now you don't care about the rest of $\\Omega$, right?  You might think let's look inside T and see how much of the area is also inside V. that is exactly what we call conditional probability.}"
                  },
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Conditional Probability, Part II}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "block": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{block}{Conditional probability}"
                      },
                      [
                        "Conditional probability",
                        "\n    For events ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "A, B ",
                              {
                                "in": "\\in"
                              },
                              " ",
                              {
                                "Omega": "\\Omega"
                              }
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        " with ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "P(B) > 0"
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        ", define the ",
                        {
                          "textit": "\\textit{conditional\n      probability}"
                        },
                        " of ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "A"
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        " given ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "B"
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        " to be\n    ",
                        {
                          "displaymath": [
                            {
                              "begin": "\\["
                            },
                            [
                              "\n      P(A|B) = ",
                              {
                                "frac": "\\frac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)}"
                              },
                              "\n      "
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "\\]"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        "\n    "
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{block}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "\n    ",
                  {
                    "center": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{center}"
                      },
                      [
                        " \n      ",
                        {
                          "includegraphics": "\\includegraphics[width = 0.5\\linewidth]{./figures/a_and_b}"
                        },
                        "\n    "
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{center}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  " \n    ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Here's the formal definition.  the conditional probability of A given B is a ratio.}"
                  },
                  "\n    ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{On the top we have the intersection.  on the bottom we have all of B}"
                  },
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Conditional Probability, Part III}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "block": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{block}{Conditional probability}"
                      },
                      [
                        "Conditional probability",
                        "\n    For events ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "A, B ",
                              {
                                "in": "\\in"
                              },
                              " ",
                              {
                                "Omega": "\\Omega"
                              }
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        " with ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "P(B) > 0"
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        ", define the ",
                        {
                          "textit": "\\textit{conditional\n      probability}"
                        },
                        " of ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "A"
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        " given ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "B"
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        " to be\n    ",
                        {
                          "displaymath": [
                            {
                              "begin": "\\["
                            },
                            [
                              "\n      P(A|B) = ",
                              {
                                "frac": "\\frac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)}"
                              },
                              "\n      "
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "\\]"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        "\n    "
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{block}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "\n    ",
                  {
                    "center": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{center}"
                      },
                      [
                        " \n      ",
                        {
                          "includegraphics": "\\includegraphics[width = 0.5\\linewidth]{./figures/a_given_b}"
                        },
                        "\n    "
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{center}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  " \n    ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{The idea is we're dropping everything in the sample space outside of B - it's not relevant, and then we have to rescale the probability so everything adds up to 1.}"
                  },
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Conditional Probability, Part IV}"
                  },
                  "\n      ",
                  {
                    "block": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{block}{Multiplicative Law of Probability}"
                      },
                      [
                        "Multiplicative Law of Probability",
                        "\n      Rearranging the conditional probability statement minimally\n      produces the ",
                        {
                          "textit": "\\textit{Multiplicative Law of Probability}"
                        },
                        ".\n\n      For ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "A, B ",
                              {
                                "in": "\\in"
                              },
                              " ",
                              {
                                "Omega": "\\Omega"
                              }
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        " with ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "P(B) > 0"
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        ",\n\n      ",
                        {
                          "displaymath": [
                            {
                              "begin": "\\["
                            },
                            [
                              "\n        P(A|B)P(B) = P(A ",
                              {
                                "cap": "\\cap"
                              },
                              " B) ",
                              {
                                "pause": "\\pause"
                              },
                              " = P(B|A)P(A)\n      "
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "\\]"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        "\n    "
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{block}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "\n    ",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{\\paul{Suggest deleting the text and just talking through it, this one's pretty simple.}}"
                  },
                  "\n",
                  "\n",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{This is an important relationship.  It gives us an intuitive way to compute the probability that A AND B occur. }"
                  },
                  "\n",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{First, you write down the probability that A occurs.  then, you assume that A has occurred, and you multiply by the probability, which is conditional, that B also occurs.}"
                  },
                  "\n",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{\\paul{Also suggest handwriting the P(B|A)P(A).  we're going to use that to prove a very famous rule, called Bayes' Rule}}"
                  },
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "section": "\\section{Learnosity Check}"
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{}"
                  },
                  "\n  Suppose that the probability that a student plays volleyball is .4, the probability that the student is tall is .5, and the probability that the student is both tall and plays volleyball is .3.\n  \n  What is the conditional probability that the student plays volleyball, given that they are tall?\n  \n  ",
                  {
                    "paul": "\\paul{Answer: .6}"
                  },
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "section": "\\section{Reading: Bayes' Rule}"
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Reading: Bayes' Rule}"
                  },
                  "\n  Read from the top of page 11 to the end of page 13.\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "section": "\\section{Total Probability}"
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{In a lot of probability problems, you need to compute the probability of some complicated event.}"
                  },
                  "\n",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{That can be hard to do directly, and you want some way to break down the problem.}"
                  },
                  "\n",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{There is a famous technique that helps in a lot of cases.  it's called the law of total probability.}"
                  },
                  "\n",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{The idea is we can use a partition of $\\Omega$ to break down any event.}"
                  },
                  "\n",
                  {
                    "note": "\\note[item]{Let's see a picture and then read the law carefully...}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Total Probability, Part I}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "block": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{block}{The Law of Total Probability}"
                      },
                      [
                        "The Law of Total Probability",
                        "\n    If",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "\\ ",
                              "A_",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "1"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              ", A_",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "2"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              ", ",
                              {
                                "dots": "\\dots"
                              },
                              ", A_",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "n"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        " is a partition of ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              {
                                "Omega": "\\Omega"
                              }
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        ", and\n    if ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "B ",
                              {
                                "in": "\\in"
                              },
                              " ",
                              {
                                "Omega": "\\Omega"
                              }
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        ", then\n    ",
                        {
                          "displaymath": [
                            {
                              "begin": "\\["
                            },
                            [
                              "\n      P(B) = ",
                              {
                                "sum": "\\sum"
                              },
                              "_",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "i"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              " P(B ",
                              {
                                "cap": "\\cap"
                              },
                              " A_",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "i"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              ")\n    "
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "\\]"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        "\n    If there is a positive probability for each partition ",
                        {
                          "$": [
                            {
                              "begin": "$"
                            },
                            [
                              "A_",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "i"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "$"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        ",\n    then by the ",
                        {
                          "textit": "\\textit{Multiplicative Law of Probability}"
                        },
                        "\n    ",
                        {
                          "displaymath": [
                            {
                              "begin": "\\["
                            },
                            [
                              "\n      P(B) = ",
                              {
                                "sum": "\\sum"
                              },
                              "_",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "i"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              " P(B | A_",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "i"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              ")P(A_",
                              {
                                "BraceGroup": [
                                  {
                                    "begin": "{"
                                  },
                                  [
                                    "i"
                                  ],
                                  {
                                    "end": "}"
                                  }
                                ]
                              },
                              ")\n    "
                            ],
                            {
                              "end": "\\]"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        "\n  "
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{block}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "\n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Total Probability, Part II}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "center": [
                      {
                        "begin": "\\begin{center}"
                      },
                      [
                        "\n    ",
                        {
                          "includegraphics": "\\includegraphics[width=0.75\\linewidth]{./figures/total_probability_0}"
                        },
                        "\n  "
                      ],
                      {
                        "end": "\\end{center}"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  " \n"
                ],
                {
                  "end": "\\end{frame}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            "\n",
            {
              "frame": [
                {
                  "begin": "\\begin{frame}"
                },
                [
                  "\n  ",
                  {
                    "frametitle": "\\frametitle{Total Probability, Part III}"
                  },
                  "\n  ",
                  {
